// S175 Scenario B: recovery before collapse (the dampener).
//
// Purpose: a tired, danger-averse agent starts co-located with a hostile at the
// "Wilds", where every Sleep attempt is interrupted via HostileProximity. With
// a high danger weight and zero courage the agent flees along the short edge to
// the safe "Haven", where no hostile is present, and rough-sleeps successfully.
// Rough sleep there recovers enough fatigue to drop below the critical
// threshold, so DeprivationExposure.fatigue_critical_ticks resets to 0 and no
// Exhaustion wound is ever created. This proves the collapse path is escapable
// (FND-11 dampener): repeated partial recovery genuinely prevents collapse.
(
    seed: 175002,
    compaction_interval: 0,
    places: [
        (
            name: "Wilds",
            tags: [Camp],
        ),
        (
            name: "Haven",
            tags: [Camp],
        ),
    ],
    edges: [
        (from: "Wilds", to: "Haven", travel_ticks: 3, bidirectional: true),
    ],
    hostilities: [
        (subject: "Aster", target: "Watcher"),
        (subject: "Watcher", target: "Aster"),
    ],
    agents: [
